# Vulnerabilities and misconfigurations ignored, each with its reason and its
# re-audit date. Trivy's plain .trivyignore has no per-path scoping (only
# .trivyignore.yaml does, and scripts/security-scan.sh never passes
# --ignorefile, so only the default ".trivyignore", this file, is read): an
# ID listed here is silenced for the whole tree this hook scans (this
# repository plus its submodules), not just for the one file that earned the
# exception.
#
# AVD-DS-0002 (HIGH, "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with
# non-root user"): llm-station-cuda/bench/harness/benchrun.Dockerfile only,
# same exception and same reasoning as that submodule's own .trivyignore
# (read there for the detail): its containers talk to the HOST docker
# daemon over /var/run/docker.sock, whose owning GID is not the same number
# on every host (Docker Desktop's VM here, a Linux station's docker group
# elsewhere), so a non-root user baked in at build time cannot be given
# access to it without either widening the socket's own permissions or an
# entrypoint script that mutates a host resource at container start, both
# worse than the finding itself. Every other Dockerfile under
# llm-station-cuda/bench/harness/ (agent, aider, bfcl, lcb, livebench,
# longbench, ruler) runs as a real non-root user; this is the one exception.
# Re-audit: 2027-03-01, or sooner if Docker ships a portable way to join an
# arbitrary host GID from a Dockerfile without an entrypoint script.
AVD-DS-0002
